<Layout title="7th Grade">
  <LinkList slot="sidebar" items={academicsYears} orientation="vertical" />
<p>Seventh grade was the year I discovered how much I love history, and also how I like to learn math best.</p>

<p>My favorite class was History. Seventh grade in California is World History: Medieval and Early Modern Times, so we traveled from the fall of Rome to the Enlightenment. Along the way we studied the rise of Islam, China, and feudal Japan, the West African kingdoms of Ghana and Mali, and the Maya, Aztec, and Inca. Then we came back to Europe for the Middle Ages, the Renaissance, the Reformation, the Scientific Revolution, and the Age of Exploration. I liked seeing how trade, ideas, and inventions moved between all of these places and connected them.</p>

<p>I took Algebra, which was taught as a flipped classroom. Instead of listening to a lecture in class and doing problems at home, we watched the lecture the night before. Then we spent class time working through problems together. I loved it. When I got stuck, I could get help right away instead of being alone with my homework, and I got a lot more practice actually solving problems.</p>

<p>I stayed in Orchestra and kept playing cello.</p>

<p>I also took my second year of French. It covered the second semester of high school French 1, so by the end of the year I had finished the whole first-year high school course.</p>

</Layout>
